{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-1329","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1896","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1897","text":": Cross-Cutting Governance for Agents"}]},{"id":"blk-1330","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1898","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-1899","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1900","text":" capability family represents an agent's ability to "},{"id":"spn-1901","marks":["bold"],"text":"enforce policy, verify identity, emit telemetry, manage cost budgets, and escalate to humans"},{"id":"spn-1902","text":" — the cross-cutting governance concerns that apply to every other primitive."}]},{"id":"blk-1331","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1903","text":"In the [&] Protocol, "},{"id":"spn-1904","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1905","text":" is the sixth primitive (cross-cutting over four cognitive + one sensorimotor):"}]},{"id":"blk-1332","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1334","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1906","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-1907","text":" — what the agent knows"}]}],"id":"blk-1333","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1336","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1908","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"},{"id":"spn-1909","text":" — how the agent decides"}]}],"id":"blk-1335","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1338","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1910","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-1911","text":" — when things happen"}]}],"id":"blk-1337","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1340","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1912","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"},{"id":"spn-1913","text":" — where things are"}]}],"id":"blk-1339","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1342","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1914","marks":["code"],"text":"&body"},{"id":"spn-1915","text":" — how the agent is instantiated in an environment (perception, action, affordance)"}]}],"id":"blk-1341","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1344","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1916","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1917","text":" — who is acting, under what rules, at what cost"}]}],"id":"blk-1343","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1345","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1918","text":"Unlike the five other primitives, which each model a distinct cognitive or sensorimotor domain, "},{"id":"spn-1919","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1920","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-1921","marks":["bold"],"text":"cross-cutting"},{"id":"spn-1922","text":". It does not exist in isolation — it wraps, constrains, and observes the others. Every "},{"id":"spn-1923","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-1924","text":" operation can emit telemetry. Every "},{"id":"spn-1925","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"},{"id":"spn-1926","text":" decision can trigger escalation. Every "},{"id":"spn-1927","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"},{"id":"spn-1928","text":" action can be identity-verified. Every "},{"id":"spn-1929","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-1930","text":" forecast can be budget-checked. Every "},{"id":"spn-1931","marks":["code"],"text":"&body"},{"id":"spn-1932","text":" action can be affordance-filtered and authorization-gated."}]},{"id":"blk-1346","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1933","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1347","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1934","text":"Why "},{"id":"spn-1935","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1936","text":" exists as a first-class primitive"}]},{"id":"blk-1348","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1937","text":"Agent governance is the most underfunded and underspecified area of AI infrastructure. As of 2025, only $414M has been invested across all dedicated AI safety/governance startups — less than 5% of total AI security investment."}]},{"id":"blk-1349","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1938","text":"Yet Gartner predicts 40% of agentic AI projects will be scrapped by 2027, primarily due to governance failures:"}]},{"id":"blk-1350","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1352","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1939","text":"agents that exceed cost budgets with no enforcement mechanism"}]}],"id":"blk-1351","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1354","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1940","text":"agents that impersonate other agents with no identity verification"}]}],"id":"blk-1353","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1356","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1941","text":"agents that make high-stakes decisions with no human escalation path"}]}],"id":"blk-1355","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1358","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1942","text":"agents that operate opaquely with no telemetry or audit trail"}]}],"id":"blk-1357","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1360","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1943","text":"multi-agent systems where no one knows which agent did what"}]}],"id":"blk-1359","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1361","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1944","text":"These are not feature requests. They are "},{"id":"spn-1945","marks":["bold"],"text":"enterprise-blocking gaps"},{"id":"spn-1946","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-1362","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1947","text":"Treating governance as a first-class capability — rather than an afterthought bolted onto application code — allows the protocol to express:"}]},{"id":"blk-1363","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1948","text":"that an agent has governance constraints at all"}]}],"id":"blk-1364","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1949","text":"what kind of governance it has (telemetry, escalation, identity)"}]}],"id":"blk-1366","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1369","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1950","text":"which provider implements each governance concern"}]}],"id":"blk-1368","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1371","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1951","text":"how governance composes with memory, reasoning, time, space, and body"}]}],"id":"blk-1370","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1373","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1952","text":"what events, budgets, and escalation rules are enforced"}]}],"id":"blk-1372","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1374","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1953","text":"Without "},{"id":"spn-1954","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1955","text":", governance tends to be hidden inside ad hoc middleware, provider-specific plugins, or manual compliance processes. The result is architecture that works in demos but fails in production."}]},{"id":"blk-1375","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1956","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1376","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1957","text":"What "},{"id":"spn-1958","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1959","text":" means in the protocol"}]},{"id":"blk-1377","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1960","text":"At the protocol level, "},{"id":"spn-1961","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1962","text":" is not a vendor, dashboard, or compliance tool."}]},{"id":"blk-1378","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1963","text":"It is a "},{"id":"spn-1964","marks":["bold"],"text":"capability interface family"},{"id":"spn-1965","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-1379","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1966","text":"That means:"}]},{"id":"blk-1380","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1382","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1967","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry"},{"id":"spn-1968","text":" is a protocol capability"}]}],"id":"blk-1381","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1384","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1969","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience"},{"id":"spn-1970","text":" is one provider that may satisfy it"}]}],"id":"blk-1383","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1386","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1971","text":"another provider could also satisfy "},{"id":"spn-1972","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry"},{"id":"spn-1973","text":" if it implements the same contract"}]}],"id":"blk-1385","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1387","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1974","text":"This separation is important."}]},{"id":"blk-1388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1975","text":"If governance were modeled only as provider-specific configuration, then changing your observability stack would require rewriting your agent declarations. By modeling "},{"id":"spn-1976","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1977","text":" as an interface family, the protocol stays portable."}]},{"id":"blk-1389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1978","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1390","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1979","text":"Common "},{"id":"spn-1980","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-1981","text":" subtypes"}]},{"id":"blk-1391","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1982","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry"}]},{"id":"blk-1392","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1983","text":"Represents the observability backbone: structured event emission, metric queries, and budget enforcement."}]},{"id":"blk-1393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1984","text":"Typical concerns:"}]},{"id":"blk-1394","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1396","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1985","text":"emitting structured telemetry events (OpenTelemetry-compatible)"}]}],"id":"blk-1395","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1398","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1986","text":"tracking token consumption and cost per task and per period"}]}],"id":"blk-1397","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1400","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1987","text":"enforcing budget limits from Delegatic policy trees"}]}],"id":"blk-1399","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1402","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1988","text":"querying historical telemetry for audit and analysis"}]}],"id":"blk-1401","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1404","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1989","text":"detecting anomalous agent behavior via cost or usage patterns"}]}],"id":"blk-1403","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1405","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1990","text":"This is the subtype most relevant to cost management, observability, and compliance."}]},{"id":"blk-1406","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-1991","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.escalation"}]},{"id":"blk-1407","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1992","text":"Represents the human-in-the-loop bridge: structured handoff from autonomous operation to human review."}]},{"id":"blk-1408","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1993","text":"Typical concerns:"}]},{"id":"blk-1409","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1411","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1994","text":"escalating when confidence falls below a threshold"}]}],"id":"blk-1410","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1995","text":"escalating when cost exceeds a budget"}]}],"id":"blk-1412","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1415","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1996","text":"escalating when a hard governance boundary is approached"}]}],"id":"blk-1414","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1417","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1997","text":"escalating when policy explicitly requires human approval"}]}],"id":"blk-1416","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1419","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1998","text":"tracking escalation history and response patterns"}]}],"id":"blk-1418","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-1999","text":"This subtype matters whenever autonomous operation must have a safety valve."}]},{"id":"blk-1421","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2000","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.identity"}]},{"id":"blk-1422","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2001","text":"Represents cross-runtime agent identity: verification, registration, and trust."}]},{"id":"blk-1423","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2002","text":"Typical concerns:"}]},{"id":"blk-1424","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1426","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2003","text":"verifying that an agent is who it claims to be (manifest hash, spec hash)"}]}],"id":"blk-1425","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1428","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2004","text":"registering agent identity on publish or deployment"}]}],"id":"blk-1427","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1430","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2005","text":"resolving agent identity from an ID or manifest reference"}]}],"id":"blk-1429","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1432","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2006","text":"preventing agent impersonation in multi-agent systems"}]}],"id":"blk-1431","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1434","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2007","text":"associating governance policies with verified identities"}]}],"id":"blk-1433","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1435","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2008","text":"This subtype is essential for multi-agent systems where trust between agents is not assumed."}]},{"id":"blk-1436","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2009","text":"Future subtype candidates"}]},{"id":"blk-1437","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2010","text":"As the protocol evolves, additional governance subtypes may emerge:"}]},{"id":"blk-1438","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1440","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2011","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.audit"},{"id":"spn-2012","text":" — dedicated audit trail management"}]}],"id":"blk-1439","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1442","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2013","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.consent"},{"id":"spn-2014","text":" — user consent and data governance"}]}],"id":"blk-1441","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1444","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2015","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.compliance"},{"id":"spn-2016","text":" — regulatory compliance checks"}]}],"id":"blk-1443","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1446","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2017","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.rate_limit"},{"id":"spn-2018","text":" — fine-grained rate limiting per capability"}]}],"id":"blk-1445","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2019","text":"The protocol should stay conservative at the primitive level and extensible at the subtype level."}]},{"id":"blk-1448","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2020","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1449","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2021","text":"What problems "},{"id":"spn-2022","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2023","text":" solves"}]},{"id":"blk-1450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2024","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2025","text":" gives the protocol a standard place to express capabilities like:"}]},{"id":"blk-1451","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1453","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2026","text":"tracking what every agent does and what it costs"}]}],"id":"blk-1452","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1455","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2027","text":"enforcing budget limits across an org hierarchy"}]}],"id":"blk-1454","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1457","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2028","text":"verifying agent identity before allowing collaboration"}]}],"id":"blk-1456","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2029","text":"escalating to humans when confidence or cost thresholds are crossed"}]}],"id":"blk-1458","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1461","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2030","text":"auditing the full provenance chain of a decision"}]}],"id":"blk-1460","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1463","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2031","text":"detecting and preventing adversarial behavior (OS-007)"}]}],"id":"blk-1462","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1464","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2032","text":"These are especially important when agents operate autonomously, at scale, across organizational boundaries."}]},{"id":"blk-1465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2033","text":"Example:"}]},{"id":"blk-1466","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2034","text":"A fleet management agent optimizes delivery routes. Without "},{"id":"spn-2035","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2036","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-1467","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1469","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2037","text":"No one knows how many tokens it consumed this month"}]}],"id":"blk-1468","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1471","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2038","text":"No one can verify it's the same agent that was tested and approved"}]}],"id":"blk-1470","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1473","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2039","text":"If it encounters an edge case it can't handle, it either hallucinates or fails silently"}]}],"id":"blk-1472","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1475","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2040","text":"If it exceeds the cost budget, there's no enforcement mechanism"}]}],"id":"blk-1474","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1476","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2041","text":"With "},{"id":"spn-2042","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry + &govern.identity + &govern.escalation"},{"id":"spn-2043","text":":"}]},{"id":"blk-1477","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1479","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2044","text":"Every route optimization emits a telemetry event with token count and cost"}]}],"id":"blk-1478","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1481","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2045","text":"The agent's identity is verified against its FleetPrompt manifest on deployment"}]}],"id":"blk-1480","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1483","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2046","text":"When confidence drops below 0.6, it escalates to a human dispatcher"}]}],"id":"blk-1482","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1485","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2047","text":"When cost exceeds "},{"id":"spn-2048","marks":["code"],"text":"max_cost_usd_per_task"},{"id":"spn-2049","text":", the operation is rejected with a clear budget error"}]}],"id":"blk-1484","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1486","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2050","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1487","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2051","text":"How "},{"id":"spn-2052","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2053","text":" differs from the governance block"}]},{"id":"blk-1488","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2054","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-2055","marks":["code"],"text":"ampersand.json"},{"id":"spn-2056","text":" "},{"id":"spn-2057","marks":["code"],"text":"governance"},{"id":"spn-2058","text":" block declares "},{"id":"spn-2059","marks":["bold"],"text":"what rules apply"},{"id":"spn-2060","text":" (hard constraints, soft preferences, escalation thresholds)."}]},{"id":"blk-1489","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2061","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-2062","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2063","text":" capability declares "},{"id":"spn-2064","marks":["bold"],"text":"which systems enforce those rules"},{"id":"spn-2065","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-1490","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2066","text":"They are complementary:"}]},{"id":"blk-1491","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"capabilities\": {\n    \"&govern.telemetry\": {\n      \"provider\": \"opensentience\",\n      \"config\": { \"org_id\": \"org_acme\" }\n    },\n    \"&govern.escalation\": {\n      \"provider\": \"opensentience\",\n      \"config\": { \"timeout_seconds\": 300 }\n    }\n  },\n  \"governance\": {\n    \"hard\": [\"Never exceed $50 per task\"],\n    \"escalate_when\": {\n      \"confidence_below\": 0.7,\n      \"cost_exceeds_usd\": 50\n    },\n    \"autonomy\": {\n      \"level\": \"advise\",\n      \"budget\": {\n        \"max_cost_usd_per_task\": 50,\n        \"max_tokens_per_period\": 1000000\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}"},{"id":"blk-1492","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2067","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-2068","marks":["code"],"text":"governance"},{"id":"spn-2069","text":" block is the "},{"id":"spn-2070","marks":["bold"],"text":"policy declaration"},{"id":"spn-2071","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-2072","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2073","text":" capabilities are the "},{"id":"spn-2074","marks":["bold"],"text":"enforcement mechanisms"},{"id":"spn-2075","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-1493","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2076","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1494","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2077","text":"How "},{"id":"spn-2078","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2079","text":" composes with the other primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-1495","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2080","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2081","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-2082","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"}]},{"id":"blk-1496","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2083","text":"Every memory operation can emit telemetry. Memory consolidation cycles can be budget-checked. Knowledge graph mutations can trigger identity verification for the writing agent."}]},{"id":"blk-1497","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2084","text":"Together they support:"}]},{"id":"blk-1498","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1500","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2085","text":"tracking which agent wrote which knowledge"}]}],"id":"blk-1499","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1502","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2086","text":"enforcing storage budgets"}]}],"id":"blk-1501","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1504","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2087","text":"auditing knowledge provenance"}]}],"id":"blk-1503","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1505","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2088","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2089","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-2090","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"}]},{"id":"blk-1506","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2091","text":"Every deliberation can be cost-tracked. High-stakes decisions can trigger escalation. Voting agents can be identity-verified before participating."}]},{"id":"blk-1507","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2092","text":"Together they support:"}]},{"id":"blk-1508","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1510","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2093","text":"budget-bounded deliberation"}]}],"id":"blk-1509","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1512","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2094","text":"human review of critical decisions"}]}],"id":"blk-1511","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1514","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2095","text":"preventing impersonation in multi-agent voting"}]}],"id":"blk-1513","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1515","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2096","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2097","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-2098","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"}]},{"id":"blk-1516","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2099","text":"Temporal forecasts and anomaly detections can emit telemetry. Expensive SSM inference can be budget-checked. Anomaly thresholds can trigger escalation when they exceed governance bounds."}]},{"id":"blk-1517","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2100","text":"Together they support:"}]},{"id":"blk-1518","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1520","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2101","text":"cost tracking for temporal intelligence operations"}]}],"id":"blk-1519","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1522","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2102","text":"degraded-mode fallback when compute budget is exhausted"}]}],"id":"blk-1521","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1524","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2103","text":"human review of high-impact temporal predictions"}]}],"id":"blk-1523","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1525","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2104","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2105","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-2106","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"}]},{"id":"blk-1526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2107","text":"Route optimizations can emit telemetry with compute cost. Geofence boundary crossings can trigger escalation. Fleet operations agents can be identity-verified before accessing sensitive location data."}]},{"id":"blk-1527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2108","text":"Together they support:"}]},{"id":"blk-1528","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1530","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2109","text":"spatial operation cost tracking"}]}],"id":"blk-1529","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1532","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2110","text":"compliance escalation on boundary violations"}]}],"id":"blk-1531","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1534","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2111","text":"identity-gated access to fleet data"}]}],"id":"blk-1533","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1535","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2112","text":"Full composition: all six primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-1536","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"stream_data\n  |> &time.anomaly.detect()\n  |> &govern.telemetry.emit()\n  |> &space.fleet.enrich()\n  |> &govern.telemetry.budget_check()\n  |> &memory.graph.enrich()\n  |> &reason.argument.evaluate()\n  |> &body.browser.affordances()     # policy-filtered action set\n  |> &govern.escalation.authorize()  # authorize destructive body actions\n  |> &body.browser.act()\n  |> &govern.escalation.escalate()   # if confidence < threshold"},{"id":"blk-1537","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2113","text":"This pipeline shows how "},{"id":"spn-2114","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2115","text":" weaves through the other five primitives — not as a separate stage, but as an observability and enforcement layer that accompanies every operation, including "},{"id":"spn-2116","marks":["code"],"text":"&body.*"},{"id":"spn-2117","text":" affordance filtering and action authorization."}]},{"id":"blk-1538","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2118","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1539","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2119","text":"Typical providers"}]},{"id":"blk-1540","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2120","marks":["code"],"text":"opensentience"}]},{"id":"blk-1541","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2121","text":"The primary runtime enforcement provider. Implements:"}]},{"id":"blk-1542","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1544","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2122","text":"OS-006: Agent Governance Shim (permission engine, lifecycle, autonomy levels)"}]}],"id":"blk-1543","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1546","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2123","text":"OS-007: Adversarial Robustness (identity verification, budget enforcement, circuit breakers)"}]}],"id":"blk-1545","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1548","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2124","text":"OS-008: Agent Harness (pipeline enforcement, quality gates, sprint contracts, context management)"}]}],"id":"blk-1547","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1549","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2125","marks":["code"],"text":"delegatic"}]},{"id":"blk-1550","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2126","text":"The policy source provider. Provides:"}]},{"id":"blk-1551","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1553","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2127","text":"Monotonic policy inheritance (budget limits flow from root to leaf orgs)"}]}],"id":"blk-1552","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1555","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2128","text":"Budget fields: "},{"id":"spn-2129","marks":["code"],"text":"max_tokens_per_task"},{"id":"spn-2130","text":", "},{"id":"spn-2131","marks":["code"],"text":"max_cost_usd_per_period"},{"id":"spn-2132","text":", etc."}]}],"id":"blk-1554","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1557","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2133","text":"Policy merge semantics: AND for booleans, MIN for numerics, INTERSECTION for allow-lists"}]}],"id":"blk-1556","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1558","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2134","marks":["code"],"text":"fleetprompt"}]},{"id":"blk-1559","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2135","text":"The identity registry provider. Provides:"}]},{"id":"blk-1560","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1562","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2136","text":"Agent manifest registration on publish"}]}],"id":"blk-1561","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1564","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2137","text":"Identity verification for marketplace agents"}]}],"id":"blk-1563","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1566","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2138","text":"Trust score computation from test coverage + spec compliance + usage history"}]}],"id":"blk-1565","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1567","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2139","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1568","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2140","text":"Anti-patterns"}]},{"id":"blk-1569","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2141","text":"Anti-pattern 1: Treating governance as optional"}]},{"id":"blk-1570","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2142","text":"If an agent operates autonomously, governance is not optional. Skipping "},{"id":"spn-2143","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2144","text":" declarations doesn't remove governance concerns — it just makes them invisible."}]},{"id":"blk-1571","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2145","text":"Anti-pattern 2: Hardcoding budget limits in application code"}]},{"id":"blk-1572","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2146","text":"Budget limits should flow from Delegatic policy trees, not be hardcoded per agent. Use "},{"id":"spn-2147","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.telemetry.budget_check()"},{"id":"spn-2148","text":" against the policy tree."}]},{"id":"blk-1573","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2149","text":"Anti-pattern 3: Identity verification only at deploy time"}]},{"id":"blk-1574","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2150","text":"Agent identity should be verified continuously — not just when first deployed. Use "},{"id":"spn-2151","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern.identity.verify()"},{"id":"spn-2152","text":" before accepting collaboration requests."}]},{"id":"blk-1575","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2153","text":"Anti-pattern 4: Escalation as error handling"}]},{"id":"blk-1576","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2154","text":"Escalation is a governance-mandated handoff, not an error. Design escalation paths as first-class workflows, not exception handlers."}]},{"id":"blk-1577","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2155","text":"Anti-pattern 5: Telemetry without structured schemas"}]},{"id":"blk-1578","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2156","text":"Unstructured log messages are not telemetry. Use the OpenTelemetry-compatible event schema with typed fields (trace_id, agent_id, capability, tokens_consumed, cost_usd_estimated)."}]},{"id":"blk-1579","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2157","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-1580","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-2158","text":"Summary"}]},{"id":"blk-1581","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2159","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2160","text":" is the protocol's answer to the question:"}]},{"id":"blk-1582","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2161","marks":["bold"],"text":"How does an agent operate safely, transparently, and within bounds?"}]},{"id":"blk-1583","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2162","text":"It matters because autonomous agents without governance are demos, not products."}]},{"id":"blk-1584","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2163","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2164","text":" makes governance:"}]},{"id":"blk-1585","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1587","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2165","text":"explicit in the declaration"}]}],"id":"blk-1586","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1589","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2166","text":"separable from providers"}]}],"id":"blk-1588","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1591","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2167","text":"contract-aware"}]}],"id":"blk-1590","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1593","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2168","text":"composable with memory, time, space, and reason"}]}],"id":"blk-1592","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1595","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2169","text":"enforceable"}]}],"id":"blk-1594","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1597","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2170","text":"auditable"}]}],"id":"blk-1596","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-1599","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2171","text":"compilable into downstream agent artifacts"}]}],"id":"blk-1598","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-1600","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2172","text":"If "},{"id":"spn-2173","marks":["code"],"text":"&memory"},{"id":"spn-2174","text":" helps the agent remember, and "},{"id":"spn-2175","marks":["code"],"text":"&reason"},{"id":"spn-2176","text":" helps it decide, and "},{"id":"spn-2177","marks":["code"],"text":"&time"},{"id":"spn-2178","text":" helps it understand change, and "},{"id":"spn-2179","marks":["code"],"text":"&space"},{"id":"spn-2180","text":" helps it stay grounded in the world,"}]},{"id":"blk-1601","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-2181","text":"then "},{"id":"spn-2182","marks":["code"],"text":"&govern"},{"id":"spn-2183","text":" ensures it does all of that "},{"id":"spn-2184","marks":["bold"],"text":"safely, transparently, and within the rules"},{"id":"spn-2185","text":"."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraphdiqvqmhk7ot3hss4ymn3fzwflqgxoujq2cwfwm2xt7b6t2dqza","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}